#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129967} :activity/id #uuid "df9a25dc-813f-52ef-bbe9-65001555ffea" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129967 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130348 :tutorial/content "Recall that the matrices $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}$ and $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}$ of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T} : V \\to V$ relative to two bases $\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}$ of a vector space $V$ are different.\n\nIf we are given the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}},$ how do we find the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}?$\nTo find $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}},$ we use the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{\\small {\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\to {\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}}$ from $\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}$ to ${\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}.$\n\nThe diagram below is a commutative diagram that shows how a change of basis works at each step.\n\n![](images/df/dff02d9f46eb7ded23f418765a50dd1971145cd0e585a82beeef1a45812df8a7.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. So algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFor instance, if $[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, we use this formula to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the formula for $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} = P_{\\small{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}}^{-1} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** Alternatively, if we know the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{\\small {\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} \\to {\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}}$ from $\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B},$ we can construct a similar diagram:\n\n![](images/d6/d6cd195ccd42804ea91debabd23563bb0f6903fdd1b5d708b712c75417fff2a9.png)\n\nFrom this, we can derive the equation\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}\\to{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}}^{-1} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}\\to{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}}.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} =\n\tP_{\\small{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}\\to{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}\\to{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}}^{-1}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "daf756b8-28df-5435-a304-0c32de77cc02" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3585 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "997bad3a-19a8-5b8c-ba06-b960fea4fabc" :step/math-academy-id 20144 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130108}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129968 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128941 :question/id #uuid "76ff3ea8-e07c-5dba-a9af-a4f68b03fadb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5516"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049548} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129630} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129639} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326682} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360752} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360753} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375096} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388702} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395222} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395229} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395236} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419683}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "a9f19301-a016-578d-9241-cc7262d6f30f" :step/math-academy-id 20145 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129970}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129969 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130349 :tutorial/content "Consider the bases $\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\, \\ldots, \\, \\mathbf{b}_n \\}$ and $\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}=\\{ \\mathbf{c}_1, \\, \\ldots, \\, \\mathbf{c}_n \\}$ of a vector space $V,$ and the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}$ of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with respect to the basis $\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}.$\nThen the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis ${\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} =P_{\\small {\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\to {\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small {\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\to {\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere $P_{\\small {\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}} \\to {\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}}$ is the change of basis matrix from ${\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}$ to ${\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}.$\n\nWhen written in expanded form, this formula becomes:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}| &  & | \\\\ \\,[T(\\,{c}_{1}\\,)]_{C} & \\,\\,\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,\\,\\, & [T(\\,{c}_{n}\\,)]_{C}\\, \\\\ | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "f7eacd50-63e4-53d3-9c15-d3a1b6a42ad1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3586 :tutorial/title "The Expanded Form of the Change of Basis"} :step/id #uuid "22fcb777-1e74-5081-b738-034b4f36efdc" :step/math-academy-id 20146 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130010}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129970 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128942 :question/id #uuid "4b287ac7-7569-59bc-a319-0e62996083bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5517"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129641} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129642} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272105} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360754} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360755} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360756} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375598} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392198} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395243} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419684}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"} :step/id #uuid "ec690891-eb4f-5c61-8dfc-bd14969e4bcd" :step/math-academy-id 20147 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129969}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130010 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128973 :question/id #uuid "5e4b6303-8ec5-5ba6-ba1d-3b28ff8924b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5897"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129697} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129701} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272110} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326717} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360776} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360777} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360778} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375116} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395256} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395263} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419685}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"} :step/id #uuid "b6ae143c-69c0-50ab-a964-29c6f8f34d83" :step/math-academy-id 21621} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130108 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129032 :question/id #uuid "c269a1d0-a47c-5f5c-96d8-4da2ecd35a48" :question/math-academy-id "e-8563"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050008}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129640} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129656} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272063} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326833} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360747} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360748} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360749} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360750} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419686}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"} :step/id #uuid "1481fd15-5d4d-5662-9141-ebd88670e6fc" :step/math-academy-id 31802 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129968}}] :activity/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186129357}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419688} :activity/id #uuid "a3e8a2c7-af14-540f-a7b1-76dc269d676b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419687 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b6934d8-eaf0-5f13-b06a-71ac2a0dc0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419660} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419667} {:answer/id #uuid "8f47a664-a9ad-5deb-90c8-17a7a38adab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419671} {:answer/id #uuid "d0704113-7386-54ca-ad0c-7578acd9ac62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -11 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419676} {:answer/id #uuid "dc81c6b4-cc09-56a5-916c-e323cc4197ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419678}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419667} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c807d8-09ff-597f-a633-55d26150ec43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "662e0d41-a6b8-58b3-ad4a-e835c48f17e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97118" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0b2e1e0a-a93e-5b2b-ba4a-b6011da00e9b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419689}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419688 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129640 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f542f252-cabb-5ae6-be52-71ede74205d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127322} {:answer/id #uuid "f86e2a77-e373-53ff-91da-4afcea8bff3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127323} {:answer/id #uuid "01af984e-b98d-5360-becd-55598849a21e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127324} {:answer/id #uuid "2360d955-fc90-55ae-8391-a0ca33c5c286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127325} {:answer/id #uuid "68dce08e-1ffa-5ce3-a38e-daf6da264321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186127325} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab4619b-148b-5109-bb9a-98dd96196200" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a7452af-fe2e-5944-8a03-a396c12645a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-38360" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "1b0f643e-dd6c-5eaf-875c-1b54d4c6e171" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419690}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419689 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094350f2-e017-53e0-b0e9-5075268dbe4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419659} {:answer/id #uuid "248c47da-3dc5-5333-809d-acf62be00f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -12 \\\\ 7 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419663} {:answer/id #uuid "7d527527-44f7-5758-b7fd-4c2cd30a0912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419670} {:answer/id #uuid "c7cdd80b-8123-585f-9ada-143e7f38d137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419674} {:answer/id #uuid "cd75b99f-ca84-5149-9b32-732c0d712c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -18 \\\\ -9 & -16\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419675}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419663} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3a3177-a079-5cdb-a624-7225c5f182a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7afd5a54-c223-5e70-9582-9406545b2d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-97279" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]},\\,C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -12 \\\\ 7 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "49084fac-fe76-5f2f-8b13-058b89e81921" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419691}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419690 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12910645-377d-54ef-bc0b-422296caf8f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419661} {:answer/id #uuid "2090546c-8891-5b10-af98-9204905ac08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419662} {:answer/id #uuid "27f9e9c7-23c3-5ee6-82bd-1ed602f60cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419664} {:answer/id #uuid "39e6d5c4-ef80-5978-98b7-b10c7c9e811a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419665} {:answer/id #uuid "da77cae2-0a6d-576c-9bbf-669849034a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419677}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419662} :answer-field/id #uuid "14b5fd09-d567-55da-9493-1ac629b8d62a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e737a421-d643-51f0-9d67-b9556fcc15c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-97060" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "9a18e940-4aa2-5db0-8cbe-98d6ec06c6cd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419687}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419691 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419683 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cd07fe6-6fc8-5bf5-a02a-2d9be90b12af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419666} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419668} {:answer/id #uuid "6431b86f-886e-5d1c-a26b-505391b5eaa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ 14 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419669} {:answer/id #uuid "9029cfa0-da2b-5680-a6e9-bd10f503ed2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 10 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419672} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bd80ae-8e71-5474-9567-c47f73ef5af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419673}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419668} :answer-field/id #uuid "80639a3b-2c96-57ee-bd01-981e0851478b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-140453" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bf368b08-5b21-5ea2-9201-b8d34ec52b51"}] :activity/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419658}]}
